    "summary": "`breach_tick_phases` printed `machine: unknown, 20 threads, Windows` on the owner's PC. On Windows the line now names the CPU, its cores and the RAM from the CIM (`Win32_Processor`, `Win32_ComputerSystem`, through one PowerShell call). On Linux it adds cores and RAM from `/proc/cpuinfo` and `/proc/meminfo`. A part the OS doesn't give is left out, and a CPU it can't name still reads `unknown`, so the run always goes on.",
